"twitter:image:alt" content="Mr. Bakhtawar Portfolio — Bakhtawar Khan. Personal Digital Portfolio · MBK Global."><meta property="og:image:width" content="1200"><meta property="og:image:height" content="630"><meta property="og:image:type" content="image/png"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta property="og:title" content="WhatsApp Chatbots for Businesses: Features, Use Cases, and Implementation | Bakhtawar Khan"><meta name="twitter:title" content="WhatsApp Chatbots for Businesses: Features, Use Cases, and Implementation | Bakhtawar Khan"><meta property="og:description" content="Plan a supported WhatsApp enquiry flow with clear consent, human handoff and realistic provider dependencies."><meta name="twitter:description" content="Plan a supported WhatsApp enquiry flow with clear consent, human handoff and realistic provider dependencies."><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/identity.css"><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/images/portfolio-icon-180.png"><link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest"></head><body class="academy page-lesson master-refresh"><header class="academy-header" id="top"><a class="academy-brand personal-brand" href="/"><span>Bakhtawar Khan<small>Personal Digital Portfolio · MBK Global</small></span></a><button class="academy-menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="academy-nav">Menu <span>+</span></button><nav id="academy-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href='/about'>About</a><a href='/projects'>Projects</a><a href='/services'>Services</a><a class='header-cta' href='/hire-me'>Let’s talk <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="portfolio-more"><summary>More</summary><div class="portfolio-panel"><section><h2>Professional work</h2><a href='/case-studies'>Case Studies</a><a href='/changelog'>Projects Changelog</a><a href='/delivered-project'>Process</a><a href='/resources'>Resources</a><a href='/news'>Notes</a></section><section><h2>Contact &amp; career</h2><a href='/book-a-call'>Book a Call</a><a href='/resume'>Resume / CV</a><a href='/hire-me'>Hire Me</a></section><section><h2>Content &amp; media</h2><a href='/gallery'>Gallery</a><a href='/blog'>Blog &amp; Articles</a><a href='/faq'>FAQs</a></section><section><h2>Personal brand</h2><a href='/about-muhammad-bakhtawar-khan'>Founder Profile</a><a href='/social'>Social Profiles</a><a href='/official-links'>Official Links</a></section></div></details><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch color theme">◐</button></nav></header><a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a><main id="main-content" class="academy-main"><section class="academy-page-hero expanded-hero "><div><div class="academy-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span>Field guide</div><p class="academy-kicker">Field guide / BAKHTAWAR KHAN</p><h1>WhatsApp Chatbots for Businesses: Features, Use Cases, and Implementation</h1><p class="expanded-deck">Plan a supported WhatsApp enquiry flow with clear consent, human handoff and realistic provider dependencies.</p><div class="editorial-actions"><a class='academy-text-link' href='/projects'>Explore the work ↗</a><a class='academy-text-link' href='/hire-me'>Start a conversation ↗</a></div></div></section><p class="article-disclosure">Educational guide · By Bakhtawar Khan · General guidance, not a claim of personally tested provider integrations.</p><section class="editorial-section"><div class="editorial-label">01 / FIELD NOTES</div><div><h2>Start with one customer journey</h2><p>A useful business chatbot might answer opening-hours questions, collect the category of an enquiry or route a support request. Define a narrow success condition before adding a model: for example, help a visitor reach the right person without repeating their issue. Draw the happy path and the places where a person must intervene. A long automated conversation is not necessarily a successful one.</p></div></section><section class="editorial-section"><div class="editorial-label">02 / FIELD NOTES</div><div><h2>A draft link is not a WhatsApp chatbot</h2><p>A click-to-chat link opens WhatsApp with a prepared message. It does not receive messages, deliver automated replies or maintain a support workflow. This portfolio’s project form prepares a WhatsApp draft; the visitor sends it themselves. An actual bot requires a supported Business Platform integration, authorized account access and infrastructure that can receive events and call the messaging API.</p></div></section><section class="editorial-section"><div class="editorial-label">03 / FIELD NOTES</div><div><h2>What platform approval changes</h2><p>Business onboarding, message templates, customer-service windows, pricing and account eligibility depend on current Meta rules and the chosen provider. Check the official documentation at the time of implementation rather than relying on a permanently fixed number of hours or a quoted fee in a blog post. Provider access and template approval should be explicit project dependencies, not hidden assumptions in a delivery promise.</p></div></section><section class="editorial-section"><div class="editorial-label">04 / FIELD NOTES</div><div><h2>Map the data before mapping the replies</h2><p>For a simple lead flow, a name, enquiry category and preferred callback time may be sufficient. Explain why the information is requested, where it goes and how a person can ask for deletion. Avoid collecting passwords, payment credentials or sensitive documents through a general-purpose chat. Restrict who can read conversation records and agree a retention period rather than keeping every message indefinitely.</p></div></section><section class="editorial-section"><div class="editorial-label">05 / FIELD NOTES</div><div><h2>Implement and test the failure paths</h2><p>A webhook handler should verify requests, handle repeated delivery safely and respond quickly while longer work happens separately. Track provider message status without assuming that an accepted request means a person read it. Test invalid input, expired permissions, opt-outs and handoff when nobody is available. Keep a manual alternative and a rollback plan. These are educational implementation considerations; no account approval or live integration is claimed here.</p></div></section><section class="editorial-section"><div class="editorial-label">NEXT / FROM READING TO PLANNING</div><div><h2>Choose a scoped next step.</h2><p>Refer to <a href="https://developers.facebook.com/docs/whatsapp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WhatsApp Business Platform documentation</a> for current provider requirements. Check policies and documentation again before implementation.</p><a class='academy-text-link' href='/whatsapp-chatbot-development'>Explore the service scope ↗</a> · <a class='academy-text-link' href='/resources'>Find related resources ↗</a></div></section><div data-portrait-track data-caption="The person behind the work"></div></main><footer class="academy-footer"><div><a class="academy-brand personal-brand" href="/"><span>Bakhtawar Khan<small>Personal Digital Portfolio · MBK Global</small></span></a><p>Thoughtful technology. Useful knowledge. Work in progress.</p></div><nav aria-label="Footer"><a href='/resources'>Resources</a><a href='/official-links'>Official links</a><a href='/gallery'>Gallery</a><a href='/resume'>Resume</a><a href='/faq'>FAQ</a><a href='/privacy-policy'>Privacy</a></nav><div class="academy-colophon"><span>© 2026 Bakhtawar Khan · MBK Global</span><a href="#top">Back to top ↑</a></div></footer><script defer src="/assets/js/academy.js"></script><script defer src="/assets/js/portfolio.js"></script><script defer src="/assets/js/visual-track.js"></script></body></html>